0..72 Comment "// A coherence cell: a rule between rules, its source a composite of two"
73..143 Comment "// laws spelled with `Path.step` in parentheses. The laws here nest no"
144..218 Comment "// operation, so the cell is the only member the cell layer does not read."
219..221 Comment "//"
222..288 Comment "// A category\'s own triangle and pentagon, over the composition of"
289..361 Comment "// `cat-shape.gandr`, return here once the cell layer reads an operation"
362..389 Comment "// nested in a law (#1510):"
390..392 Comment "//"
393..464 Comment "//   rule triangle : (Path.step(assoc(f, id(b), g), comp(f, unitL(g))))"
465..494 Comment "//     ==> comp(unitR(f), g);"
495..577 Comment "//   rule pentagon : (Path.step(assoc(comp(f, g), h, k), assoc(f, g, comp(h, k))))"
578..687 Comment "//     ==> (Path.step(Path.step(comp(assoc(f, g, h), k), assoc(f, comp(g, h), k)), comp(f, assoc(g, h, k))));"
689..760 Comment "/// Two steps and the shortcut between their ends: the cell relates the"
761..804 Comment "/// composite of the steps to the shortcut."
